<p class="page-kicker">Factions</p>
<h1>Chitinous Enclaves</h1>
</header>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="toc"><div class="toc-title">On this page</div><div class="toc-links"><a href="#kranov-enclave">Kranov Enclave</a><a href="#mothua-enclave">Mothua Enclave</a><a href="#ekternau-enclave">Ekternau Enclave</a></div></nav><article class="lore-page"><p>The Chitinous Enclaves are made up of various tribes of hunting bugmen scattered all throughout the world. Not much is true amongst all of the tribes other than each tribe takes great import in hunting and becoming the apex predators of their environment. Some tribes are more bug-like and some are more humanoid, but all are bug-like. A Greater Hive-Mind, the Great Mother, rules over each tribe, but not each individual. The control is enough to give each tribe a direction, though none outside of the Chitinous Enclaves know where the Great Mother originates from.</p>
<h2 id="kranov-enclave">Kranov Enclave</h2>
<p>The Chitinous Enclave doesn’t have much of a presence in Krashq’kanov, but the presence it does have is far more inhuman than most of their brethren. Their ideal prey are the great beasts of the region, Shrikes, the combat constructs who wander away from the great Monoliths, and various villages and towns.</p>
<p>Their exoskeletons are typically a glossy, obsidian black, with mud-green colorations between each outer plate of the exoskeleton. Unlike most of their brethren of the other Enclaves, the Kranov Enclave uses giant, thin, spined pincer claws and spined skeletal tails, all of which having an even tougher exoskeleton plating. As with all Enclaves, the Kranov Enclave knows that might makes right, and he who slays the greatest foes and beasts shall command the Enclave.</p>
<h2 id="mothua-enclave">Mothua Enclave</h2>
<p>The Mothua Enclave is unique among the Chitinous Enclaves in that it was among the first spawned by the Great Mother. They were among the first to walk the lands and were the first people to name themselves on those lands - Mothua - before they named the lands after themselves.</p>
<p>Thin, elegant, moth-like beings, pale as moonlight. They seem almost fragile with such slim and spindly limbs, such fragile looking wings, frail antennae, porcelain white exoskeleton plating, and human-like face plates. Their clothes weren’t hardy either, made of the soft and silky-smooth antir mycoid skins gathered and skinned from antir mushrooms. Their weapons were neither large nor bulky, either, being made of sharpened and carefully shaped and sharpened antlers, wrapped in antir mycoid skin-leather and adorned with special blue-bells or other such plants, made to never die and to remain in full bloom.</p>
<p>The Mothua Enclave, living in the eastern forests of Mothua, reside in a forest that has come to be known as the Ancient Wood. The forests here have grown strange and warped, tree canopies grown so thick that sunlight may never touch the forest floor. Here, the Mothua Enclave can outrun all, leaping from tree to tree, using strange moth-like wings to aid them in leaps, bounds, and glides. They use the vibrant antir mushrooms almost like a spider-web to track their prey or to sense intruders.</p>
<p>Their weapons drip with various poisons, though it is mostly for show. What is seen dripping is little more than flower-dyed tree sap, for the real poison seeped and soaked into the antlers themselves long ago.</p>
<p>Unlike most of the Chitinous Enclaves, the Mothua Enclave does not need to hunt the largest or most terrifying beasts, for they know what holds true power: the strange humans in their lands, able to adapt to any situation, to flood any other force or creature with such numbers that the likes of which cannot be comprehended. No, the Mothua Enclave will slink along by night in search of officers, Inquisitors, Holy Sisters, members of noble houses, and so on, aiming to assassinate those for the simple joy of watching it cripple the odd, screaming, wriggling creatures that call themselves humans.</p>
<h2 id="ekternau-enclave">Ekternau Enclave</h2>
<p>The Ekternau Enclave, residing in and around the large islands of Ekternau. They are primarily crustacean-like, not so much insectoid, unlike most of their brethren. On top of their exoskeletons, they wear the plate-like bone fragments of whales and great fish like additional armor, segmented and tethered together with whale sinew, believed to provide strength and durability.</p>
<p>They use take their old exoskeletons, break them down, and reshape them using sinew from large fish and carved driftwood to create gargantuan, odd weapons. One such weapon seen was a re-used sharpened claw mounted on a large staff, while another seen was a large slab of armor mounted on a shorter pole of driftwood, sharpened and serrated.</p>
<p>Their intelligence is above that of those like the Kranov Enclave, but below those of the Mothua Enclave. They primarily hunt great whales, squids, leviathans, and the various peoples of the Ekternau islands. Occasionally, the Ekternau Enclave will travel to the western shores of Mothua to hunt the strange, ink covered humans there. None of the humans are particularly powerful there, but their numbers are numerous enough to give the Ekternau Enclave a good time.</p></article>
